# Line endings. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so the
# Windows CI runner checks text files out with CRLF. The shader goldens are
# compared byte-for-byte against string literals (which rustc normalizes to
# LF), and the shell scripts are parsed by bash there; keep both LF on every
# checkout so the lane sees the same bytes as Linux and macOS.
*.glsl text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
